{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-amr-022-2087-research-problems-in-function-theory-p-7288357e-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T15:37:58Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-amr-022-2087-research-problems-in-function-theory-p-7288357e-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-amr-022-2087-research-problems-in-function-theory-p-7288357e-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-amr-022-2087-research-problems-in-function-theory-p-7288357e-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/AMR-022-2087"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Does there exist a non-linear entire function $g$ with wandering domain $W$ such that $\\bigcup_{n\\geq0}g^n(W)$ is bounded in $\\mathbb{C}$? It has been conjectured by Lyubich that if $g$ and $W$ exist, then $g^n(W)$ cannot converge as $n\\to\\infty$ to a fixed point of $g$. (M. R. Herman; A. Eremenko and M. Yu. Lyubich)"}, "statement_sha256": "69ab52f6b8676550ef89371d7d3f3e1114e01f9f893f14cec65c501212a60c1e"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-amr-022-2087-research-problems-in-function-theory-p-7288357e-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/AMR-022-2087"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha256":